      "content": "that's a bit surprising—specifically the part about increased sensitivity and tolerance for African Americans. i've heard some older medical texts suggest the opposite, like the idea that certain groups might actually have a higher threshold for pain or require more analgesics because they're \"tougher\" or something. is there any clinical evidence for those older theories, or are they considered debunked myths now? i just want to make sure i don't fall into any of those old clinical biases during the exam.",
