      "content": "Those older theories, known as the \"sickermann\" or \"neurasthenic\" concepts, have largely been debunked by modern research. Studies consistently show that African Americans experience increased sensitivity to painful stimuli and exhibit greater pain perceptions compared to their counterparts, not increased tolerance. These differences are quite direct and regard physiological rather than subjective.",
